Sources read (upstream code was read, not run):

  zotero     https://github.com/zotero/zotero      commit 9cbba8c4d281
             chrome/content/zotero/xpcom/data/search.js,
             data/searchConditions.js, data/collection.js (getDescendents),
             data/item.js (setField storage of date fields, itemNotes rows),
             xpcom/fulltext.js (findTextInString, findItemsWithContent,
             canSearchContent, canSearchNotes, getNoteContentSQL),
             xpcom/utilities_internal.js (normalizeForSearch),
             xpcom/collectionTreeRow.js (getSearchObject),
             xpcom/attachments.js and xpcom/annotations.js (link-mode and
             annotation-type numbers), resource/schema/system.sql
             (fileTypes, fileTypeMimeTypes), test/tests/searchTest.js and
             test/content/support.js (ported as tests/zotero_search.rs)
  utilities  https://github.com/zotero/utilities   commit 4051881d59c6
             utilities.js (allowedKeyChars, isValidObjectKey)

The test fixture's full-text strings are the text content of Zotero's test
files test/tests/data/search/{foo,foobar}.html and the output of `pdftotext`
(poppler) on test/tests/data/search/baz.pdf and test/tests/data/test.pdf
(AGPL-3.0, same copyright); the files themselves are not copied.

Each ported file carries a header naming its upstream file(s) and commit.
